  "Convert rights declarations into a workable licensing market instead of a binary open/closed web.": "Vakasamataka na ivakatakila ni dodonu me maketi ni laiseni e cakacaka, ka sega ni dua ga na web dola/sogo.",
  "Copied ✓": "Kopi Oti ✓",
  "Copy": "Kopi",
  "Correct positioning: independent research drafts, protocol proposals, and an open specification experiment.": "iTuvaki Dodonu: draft ni vakadidike tudei, ivakarau ni protocol, kei na iVakatovolei ni ivakamacala dola.",
  "Corrected an earlier default: Belgium (BE) now maps to Dutch instead of French — Flemish speakers are the country’s majority (~60%) over Walloon French speakers (~40%).": "Vakadodonutaki e dua na ivakarau makawa: na Belgium (BE) sa vakaisemati oqo ki na vosa Dutch, sega ni Vosa Vaka-Franis — na dauvosa Flemish era levu cake (~60%) mai na dauvosa Walloon Franis (~40%).",
  "Corrected an earlier default: Kazakhstan (KZ) now maps to Kazakh instead of Russian, now that a Kazakh translation exists — the same kind of fix as the earlier Belgium correction.": "Vakadodonutaki e dua na ivakarau makawa: na Kazakhstan (KZ) sa vakaisemati oqo ki na Kazakh, sega ni Rusia, ni sa tiko oti na ivakadewa Kazakh — vaka ga na kena vakadodonutaki a caka oti ena Belgium.",
  "Could AI Be Conscious?": "Could AI Be Conscious?",
  "Crawler access rules": "Lawa ni Curu ni Crawler",
  "Crawler simulator": "iVakatovolei ni Crawler",
  "Currency": "iLavo",
  "Custom tier": "Tikina Vakalomani",
  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "E ripota o Daily Nous me baleta e dua na ivola ni vola ki na Journal of Medical Ethics e vakalecai tale, ena vuku ni levu na icavuti buli, hallucinated ena AI — vata kei na iVakawekawe vakayunivesiti lasu kei na imeli sa sega tu ni cakacaka — ka a sega ni vakadodonutaki na daunivola ena gauna e solia vua na rawa me vakadodonutaka. Na tikinivola e vakatauvatana kei na Bioethics, e na kunea na leqa kevaka e cakacaka na kena dikevi vakamasini ni icavuti; ka kaya ni na leqa dina e sega ni na technology ni kunea (e dua na script nei dua e tuvala ena gauna lailai ga) ia na cakacaka wale ga ni ira na daunidikevi kei na ivakavakarau ni vola era vakalevutaka na levu ni ivola sivia na dikevi vinaka.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Kena Vakayagataki Wale na Itukutuku vs. na Isau ni AI e Trilioni Dola",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "E vakarautaka o Demis Hassabis e dua na dauveiliutaki vaka-FINRA me baleti na kena vakatakilai na model frontier: na laboratory era na vakauta na model mera dikevi ni bera ni 30 na siga ni buli, vakalomani taumada, ena dua na sala ki na kena vakadonui vakalevu ena maketi ni US.",
  "Denied": "Vakatabuya",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Template Tekivu ni Policy e Rawa ni Vakayagataki",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Template Tekivu ni Policy e Rawa ni Vakayagataki ena /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — e dua na vasite vakalailai vakamacala vata kei na tikina vakamasini taucoko, e rawa ni vakayagataki ena Cloudflare Pages se dua tale na static host.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Kena Vakayagataki na Policy Vakamasini ena Nomu Vasite",
  "Disclaimer": "iVakasala",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "E duidui mai na UI vakaitamata, SEO, se API wale, na AI Ingestion & Capability Layer e solia vei ira na vasite e dua na ivakarau vakamasini: Manifest Layer (sala ni curu me vaka /llms.txt kei /ai/manifest.json), Corpus Layer (kila e rawa ni wilikitaki ena masini), Capability Layer (iyaya e rawa ni vakayagataki ena agent), kei na Governance Layer (itukutuku ni ivu, laiseni, version). E tekivu vakastatic, ka rawa ni vakalevutaki ki na API kei na MCP. iVakasala: ena ivola oqo na AICL e vakatakila na ivakarau ni ingestion; ena tabana ni protocol ni vasite oqo na AICL e vakaibalebaletaka na Tikina ni Laiseni ni iYaya AI.",
  "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm": "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm",
  "Docs": "iVola",
  "Docs / Examples": "iVola / iVakaraitaki",
  "Document library": "Valeniivola",
  "Does AI have rights — and which framings are even coherent?": "E dodonu beka na AI — ka na cava na sala ni vakasama e macala dina?",
  "Download": "Download",
  "Draft status": "Ituvaki ni Draft",
  "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026": "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026",
  "Educational demo: HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret, showing request-bound, expiring, verifiable license tokens. Production tokens should be signed asymmetrically, with the publisher’s public key discoverable under /.well-known/.": "iVakaraitaki ni Vuli: HMAC-SHA256 ena dua na icakacaka vauci — e vakaraitaka na token ni laiseni e vauci ki na taro, e muria na gauna, ka rawa ni vakadeitaki. Na token ni cakacaka dina me sainitaki asymmetrically, ena kii dodonu ni dauveivakaraitaki e rawa ni kunei ena /.well-known/.",
  "Eight more /topics entries, this time researched by an AI agent rather than curated by hand — same rule as before: every source fetched and confirmed live, summaries an original paraphrase, before anything gets added. 14 entries total.": "E walu tale na ivola ena /topics, e vakadidikei oqo ena agent AI, sega ni kena wilika vakaitamata — vaka ga na lawa taumada: na ivavakoso yadua e kunei ka vakadeitaki tu, na ivakalekaleka e vola vou, ni bera ni kabora e dua na ka. 14 na ivola taucoko.",
  "Email": "iMeli",
